@jakearchibald @domenic would love your opinion on this if you have time from a design PoV and "does this play nice in terms of what developers would expect being used to service workers and fetch".

@mcollina @ronag would love your opinion on this from a Node.js PoV and does this play nice with user expectations with streams as incoming request is a stream.

Basically:
 - Every HTTP request in Node.js (and by extension in frameworks that inherit from it) exposes a `signal` property.
 - When the request is aborted - its signal gets aborted.

This enables code like:

```js
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  fetch(process(req.url), { signal: req.signal }).then(...);
})
```

